      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was called the Village of Vreeland until 1838, when the family sold most of the land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flat_Rock%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1925 Henry Ford built a lamp factory on the Huron River, harnessing its water power.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flat_Rock%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Flat Rock Dam was constructed to supply hydroelectricity to Ford's lamp factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
